<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jacobus Boshof</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1808">1808</a>–<a href="/years/1881">1881</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Jacobus Nicolaas Boshof</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Jacobus Boshof was the second president of the Orange Free State, from 1855 to 1859. Born in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cape-colony">Cape Colony</a>, he had been an official in Natal before his election, and he gave the young republic firmer administration. His presidency saw the first war with Moshoeshoe's <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sotho-people">Basotho</a> in 1858 and an attempt by the South African Republic under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marthinus-wessel-pretorius">Marthinus Wessel Pretorius</a> to absorb the Free State.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/jacobus-boshof.jpg" alt="Jacobus Boshof" width="320" height="413" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:JNBoshoff_litho_web.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
